nt out of hypothetical fear carries a quantifiable human toll that institutional guardians refuse to measure. When regulatory frameworks delay medical breakthroughs and material science discoveries by even 24 months, thousands of patients suffer from preventable conditions that automated intelligence could have diagnosed and cured. Precautionary delay is not a neutral stance of safety; it is an active choice to let people die of diseases while waiting for institutional committees to grant permission to heal.",
